# The Planetary Council's window (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c): the functions no click reaches, called by hand with the script
# host's open steps (the methods of the window at 0x6fec80 and of its interface part, 0xa14 into it). The window as it opens; the seat
# of faction 0 and of faction 7 drawn (nothing: neither has a seat); the calls that do nothing (the group click, the button's pass-over
# and text, and the interface part's nine and three stubs); the arrival of the human (faction 1: the window is drawn again and, with every human come, a
# notice shown); the interface's status off, which puts the window away (the buttons hidden, the window slid out and hidden), then show,
# which asks the interface for the mode again, then status on; the interface's forwarding of a button click (Yea); the mouse leaving
# a seat; and close(), which puts the buttons and the fonts away (after it nothing more is drawn). The state regions are as in
# councwin_vote.scene.
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
